@startuml architecture-components
' The components of the system and the way they are connected.
'
' A component is a unit that a caller talks to. The lines are the calls the
' components make on one another, and the three stores at the bottom are the
' state the whole system shares.

!include _style.puml
left to right direction

component "Operator console" as Console
component "REST API" as API
component "Job pipeline" as Jobs
component "Matching engine" as Match
component "Tailoring" as Tailor
component "Application workflow" as Workflow
component "Identity" as Auth
component "Evaluation" as Eval

database "Relational database" as DB
database "Vector store" as Vectors
folder "Per-user files" as Files

Console ..> API : REST over HTTP
API --> Jobs
API --> Match
API --> Tailor
API --> Workflow
API --> Auth
API --> Eval

Jobs ..> DB
Match ..> Vectors
Match ..> DB
Tailor ..> DB
Workflow ..> Files
Workflow ..> DB
Auth ..> DB
Eval ..> DB

note bottom of API
  Every request passes through the
  middleware stack and resolves its
  scope from the authenticated principal.
end note

@enduml
